<title>GERMANY: Australian producer sales key to gold price - bank.</title>
<headline>Australian producer sales key to gold price - bank.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The level of Australian producer sales in gold would determine near-term prices, Dresdner bank said in a weekly precious metals report.</p>
<p>Continued selling could breach support at $377, in which case gold may be headed for $372.</p>
<p>But the mines would base their strategy on the course of the Australian dollar which to date had offered them attractive sales opportunities.</p>
<p>London gold was fixed at $377.60 on Friday afternoon.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
